+### [Stackless Traversal](5202-stackless-traversal.md)
+Stackless Traversal is a method for traversing hierarchical volume structures (such as N3-trees or octrees) that eliminates the need for an explicit stack data structure by recalculating Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) parameters at every descent and ascent. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [DDA Tree Traversal with Mini-Stack](5244-dda-tree-traversal-with-mini-stack.md) by relying on parent pointers stored within the hierarchy to navigate, trading memory usage for computational cost. This approach is particularly advantageous in memory-constrained environments, such as early GPU architectures where dynamic array indexing forced stack data into slow local memory.
